{"chunk_id":"R3-207179-header","collection":"ran3_cr_chunks","metadata":{"source":"Qualcomm Incorporated, Nokia, Nokia Shanghai Bell","specNumber":"38.413","tdocNumber":"R3-207179","title":"Support of release on CAG subscription change"},"point_id":"6214464558691028284"}
[CR CR0484r1 for 38.413] Reason for change: At RAN3#108-3, RAN3 sent an LS to SA2 (S2-2004808/R3-204324) raising concern that the HO procedure triggered by the mobility restriction list change is a new behaviour (and that the MRL is only used to control subsequent mobility in CM-CONNECTED). SA2 has now changed their specifications as per LS sent (S2-2005904). As a result, at least in some cases as described in the CRs, the AMF requests the release of the AN connection after a CAG subscription change. However currently the existing cause values for NPN are tightly linked to access rejection only. Typical use case for release is instead when the mobility restriction is updated while the UE is in connected mode (i.e. not linked to access). Summary of change: The scope of an existing NPN cause value is extended to cover also the release use case. Note that this would already be the case anyway at access from a procedural point of view (i.e. the RAN receives a release command), but the release would happen immediately after the UE’s access. Impact analysis: This CR has isolated impact towards the previous version of the specification (same release). The impact can be considered isolated because the change only affects the PNI-NPN functionality, and because it only extends the use of an existing cause value. Consequences if not approved: No support for the flows in stage 2 specification.
